  "question": {
    "text": "The coercivity of a small magnet, where the ferromagnet gets demagnetised is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The current required to be passed in a solenoid of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and number of turns <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>, so that the magnet gets demagnetised when inside the solenoid is",
